egrated and no global verification is left unrun\n12892fc feat: /495 adopt reads a trajectory document checked against its contract, keeps it as the program's objective, creates the program and adopts its trajectory or refuses it with no program or change, then starts and conducts the change of the first ready increment, whose request carries its title, value and closure criterion\n2cb8378 test: adopting from Pi a trajectory document of three linked increments creates the program and binds the session to the change of the first increment, whose request carries its title, value and closure criterion, while a document with an unassigned global requirement or an increment missing its closure criterion is refused by name with no program, change or binding\n180d6a6 feat: a program status carries each milestone with its latest evaluation and whether the program is closed, and its text lists each increment with its status and each milestone with its verdict and what remains, in French and in English\nb1ce34d test: a program status lists each increment with its status and each milestone with its last evaluation and what remains, says the program closed once its final milestone passes, in French and in English\n507904d feat: a trajectory adoption carries the program's global requirements with their scope decisions and is refused, naming each one, when a global requirement is carried by no increment, verified by no milestone and set aside by no reasoned scope decision\n168951c test: a global requirement assigned to no increment, milestone verification or scope decision blocks the trajectory adoption, and the adoption event keeps each global requirement with its scope decision\ne47e089 docs: the story e10s04 is in progress\nprogram-entry.test.ts\nprogram-next-entry.test.ts\nprogram-increments.test.ts\nprogram-next-increment.test.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73b891a8-fc69-4dcc-bc3a-ed4ac4730d0c","uuid":"41bfa2d7-527e-4900-a935-fd9d1cf8b706","t